# OASR benchmark / serving / test environment file.
#
# Copy to `.env` and `source` before running the benchmarks or the test suite,
# so the long paths are not repeated on every command line:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     # edit paths
#     set -a; source .env; set +a
#
# `set -a` exports every assignment that follows, so the variables show up in
# child processes (Python, pytest, the spawned `oasr-server`, etc.).  The bench
# scripts read `OASR_RS_BIN`; the other variables are expanded into the CLI
# (e.g. `--ckpt-dir "$CKPT_DIR"`).  This template is tracked by git and `.env`
# is not (see .gitignore), so every path below is a placeholder: put your
# machine's absolute paths in `.env`, never in this file.

# ----- Model checkpoint + audio --------------------------------------------
# WeNet-format Conformer-CTC checkpoint directory (contains units.txt and the
# encoder/decoder weights).  Used by both `bench_engine.py` and the spawned
# `oasr-server` in `bench_service.py`.
CKPT_DIR=/path/to/models/20210610_u2pp_conformer_exp_librispeech

# Directory of mono 16 kHz .wav files to feed the bench (recurses one level).
AUDIO_DIR=/path/to/data/ljspeech-sr16k-dataset/wavs

# Optional: WFST decoder graph dir (only needed for *_wfst subroutines and
# requires `OASR_USE_K2=1` at build time).
# WFST_DIR=

# ----- Test-suite assets ----------------------------------------------------
# `pytest` does NOT read this file — `set -a; source .env; set +a` first, then
# run pytest.  Every variable below is declared in `tests/assets.py`, which
# stays the single source of truth for what each asset is and which marker file
# proves it is really present.  A missing asset skips its tests and is listed in
# the "external assets:" table at the end of the run; `--strict-assets` turns
# those skips into failures (what CI runs).
#
# Alternative to the per-asset variables below: if every asset lives under one
# tree laid out with the `relpath` names from tests/assets.py (u2pp_conformer/,
# wavs/, zipformer_ctc/, whisper_tiny/, paraformer_zh/, qwen2_audio_tiny/,
# qwen2_audio_7b/, nemotron_asr_streaming_0.6b/, lang_bpe/HLG.pt), set
# `OASR_ASSET_ROOT` to it and drop the rest.  The assets here are spread across
# several trees, so they are named one by one.  A per-asset variable always
# wins over the root.

# WeNet U2++ conformer (train.yaml + final.pt) — same dir as $CKPT_DIR above,
# which the test suite reads directly.

# Directory of 16 kHz .wav files for the engine / end-to-end tests.  Distinct
# from $AUDIO_DIR (only the benchmarks read that one), so both are set.
WAV_DIR=/path/to/data/ljspeech-sr16k-dataset/wavs

# LibriSpeech dev-clean as asrbench prepares it -- the quantization calibration
# set (`oasr quantize --calib-manifest $LIBRISPEECH_DEV_DIR/manifest.jsonl`).
#   python -m benchmarks.asrbench prepare librispeech --subset dev-clean --download
LIBRISPEECH_DEV_DIR=$HOME/.cache/oasr/asrbench/librispeech/dev-clean

# A single .wav for the CPU decoder integration tests.
AUDIO_PATH=/path/to/data/ljspeech-sr16k-dataset/wavs/LJ001-0001.wav

# icefall Zipformer CTC release (huggingface.co/k2-fsa).
ZIPFORMER_CKPT=/path/to/models/icefall-asr-librispeech-zipformer-large-cr-ctc-20241018

# icefall Zipformer pruned-RNNT release, for the `transducer` architecture.
# The dir sniffs as zipformer, so it is loaded with architecture='transducer'
# (`--architecture transducer` on bench_accuracy.py / EngineConfig.architecture).
TRANSDUCER_CKPT=/path/to/models/icefall-asr-librispeech-zipformer-2023-05-15

# icefall *causal* (streaming) Zipformer pruned-RNNT release — the one checkpoint
# that exercises streaming Zipformer on real weights.  Keep the TorchScript
# streaming export (exp/jit_script_chunk_16_left_128.pt): it is icefall's own
# streaming forward, and the streaming parity test compares against it.
STREAMING_ZIPFORMER_CKPT=/path/to/models/icefall-asr-librispeech-streaming-zipformer-2023-05-17

# HF-format Whisper (huggingface.co/openai/whisper-tiny).
WHISPER_CKPT=/path/to/models/whisper-tiny

# FunASR Paraformer (modelscope / huggingface funasr paraformer-zh).
OASR_PARAFORMER_CKPT=/path/to/models/paraformer-zh

# Tiny random Qwen2-Audio fixture (fp32 parity oracle) and the real 7B snapshot
# (huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2-Audio-7B-Instruct).
SPEECH_LLM_TINY=/path/to/models/qwen2-audio-tiny-random
SPEECH_LLM_CKPT=/path/to/models/qwen2-audio-7b-instruct

# HF-format Nemotron ASR (huggingface.co/nvidia/nemotron-3.5-asr-streaming-0.6b).
NEMOTRON_CKPT=/path/to/models/nemotron-3.5-asr-streaming-0.6b

# Silero VAD v5 weights, for `--vad-backend silero`.  The upstream TorchScript
# archive is loaded and converted directly, so there is no conversion step:
#
#   mkdir -p silero-vad && curl -L -o silero-vad/silero_vad.jit \
#     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/snakers4/silero-vad/master/src/silero_vad/data/silero_vad.jit
SILERO_VAD_DIR=/path/to/models/silero-vad

# k2 lang dir (HLG.pt + words.txt) for the CPU WFST decoder, and the decoding
# graph for the GPU WFST smoke tests (a k2 HLG.pt or a prebuilt .img).
LANG_DIR=/path/to/models/lm/20210610_u2pp_conformer_exp_librispeech/lang_bpe
OASR_TEST_FST=/path/to/models/lm/20210610_u2pp_conformer_exp_librispeech/lang_bpe/HLG.pt

# Upstream source trees used only as parity oracles.  These are also the
# defaults in tests/assets.py; set them to point somewhere else.  See the
# docstrings in tests/models/test_transformer_decoder.py and
# tests/models/arch/test_zipformer.py for what to copy in.  Both are a handful of files over HTTPS, at the revisions
# ci/modal_assets.py pins -- `modal run ci/modal_app.py::fetch_assets --only
# WENET_REF_DIR,ICEFALL_ZIPFORMER_DIR` does it for Modal, and locally:
#
#   ICE=3f848bb6d0acc970c9b294a30ca0a04a7c9c78d1
#   WEN=bda6c86ff74d3ad257234a672d8a7bc4d0f32e81
#   mkdir -p /tmp/icefall_ref /tmp/wenet_ref/transformer /tmp/wenet_ref/utils
#   for f in zipformer.py scaling.py subsampling.py; do curl -sSf \
#     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/k2-fsa/icefall/$ICE/egs/librispeech/ASR/zipformer/$f \
#     -o /tmp/icefall_ref/$f; done
#   for f in transformer/decoder.py transformer/decoder_layer.py \
#            transformer/attention.py transformer/embedding.py \
#            transformer/positionwise_feed_forward.py utils/mask.py \
#            utils/common.py; do
#     curl -sSf https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wenet-e2e/wenet/$WEN/wenet/$f \
#          -o /tmp/wenet_ref/$f; done
#
# Left unset they are simply MISSING and the parity tests skip, which is how
# they have always run here -- the two suites are 27 tests nobody was seeing.
WENET_REF_DIR=/tmp/wenet_ref
ICEFALL_ZIPFORMER_DIR=/tmp/icefall_ref

# ----- External wfst project -------------------------------------------------
# Checkout of the standalone `wfst` repo (holds python/ and data/), read by
# `benchmarks/decoders/wfst.py` and `scripts/wfst_parity_check.py` as the default
# for --graph / --logprobs / --wfst-home.  Both scripts exit with a message
# naming those flags when it is unset.
OASR_WFST_HOME=/path/to/wfst

# ----- Rust serving frontend ------------------------------------------------
# Optional: absolute path to an `oasr-server` executable for `bench_service.py`.
# Leave unset to use the `oasr-server` console script installed by `pip install`
# (resolved on $PATH), which loads the `oasr._core` extension.  Set this only to
# point at a specific build, e.g. a cargo target dir (CARGO_TARGET_DIR):
# OASR_RS_BIN=/tmp/oasr-cargo-target/release/oasr-server

# ----- asrbench (python -m benchmarks.asrbench) ----------------------------
# Paths only -- the suite's sizing comes from its profiles, which every run
# records.  Prepared datasets default to ~/.cache/oasr/asrbench, results to
# .artifacts/asrbench.  LJSPEECH_DIR is optional: `prepare ljspeech` also finds
# the corpus through $AUDIO_DIR / $WAV_DIR above.
# ASRBENCH_DATA_DIR=/path/to/data/asrbench
# ASRBENCH_RESULTS_DIR=~/.local/share/oasr/asrbench/results   # default when unset
# LJSPEECH_DIR=/path/to/data/ljspeech-sr16k-dataset

# ----- Bench defaults (optional) -------------------------------------------
# Read directly by `bench_engine.py` and `bench_service.py` — when set, these
# become the argparse defaults for the matching flag, so you can drop the flag
# from the CLI.  The CLI flag still wins when both are given.
#
#   $NUM_UTTERANCES  → --num-utterances
#   $MAX_BATCH_SIZE  → --max-batch-size
#   $CONCURRENCY     → --concurrency       (bench_service.py only)
#   $CHUNK_MS        → --chunk-ms          (bench_service.py only)
NUM_UTTERANCES=2000
MAX_BATCH_SIZE=64
CONCURRENCY=64
CHUNK_MS=640
